INTRO = ["If you are searching for ceramic braces Australia-wide, you are likely weighing up the same question thousands of Australians ask every year: how do I straighten my teeth without a mouth full of metal? Ceramic braces use tooth-coloured ceramic brackets bonded to the front of the teeth, connected by an archwire and held in place with clear or tooth-toned elastics. The result is a fixed orthodontic appliance that is far less noticeable than traditional metal braces — and, for many adults and teenagers, well worth the premium price.", "Ceramic braces are appropriate for most of the same issues as metal braces, including crooked or crowded teeth, gaps and spacing, overbites, underbites, crossbites and open bites. Across Australia, a full course of treatment typically costs between $5,000 and $9,500, with most patients paying $6,500–$8,000. In this guide, we have reviewed and ranked the top 10 ceramic braces providers in Australia — from specialist-leaning independent practices in Melbourne and Sydney to trusted national networks — so you can compare prices, locations, hours, ratings and treatment options in one place. You will also find the latest cost tables, honest answers to the most common ceramic braces questions, and a clear methodology explaining how we ranked each clinic.", "Positions 1 to 3 are paid placements with do-follow links. Positions 4 to 10 are editorial selections with no-follow links. Browse our complete directory of <a href=\"/australia/\">all dental services across Australia</a>. Read <a href=\"/methodology/\">our methodology</a> and our <a href=\"/disclosures/\">disclosures policy</a> for full transparency."]
